in_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":92.9,"_gate_piotroski":8,"_gp_piotroski":true,"_score_piotroski":88.9,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":-0.014415125004944462,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":34.2,"_gate_rev_durability":0.10441314342238073,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":77.2,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.024918320392351635,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":38.8,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.0010718138250812581,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":51.3,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.018829113924050633,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":68.6,"_gate_insider_own":0.008169999,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":5.4,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Intercontinental Exchange, Inc., together with its subsidiaries, provides technology and data to financial institutions, corporations, and government entities in the United States, the United Kingdom, the European Union, Canada, Asia Pacific, and the Middle East. It operates through three segments: Exchanges, Fixed Income and Data Services, and Mortgage Technology. The Exchanges segment operates regulated marketplace technology for the listing, trading, and clearing of an array of derivatives contracts and financial securities, such as commodities, interest rates, foreign exchange and equities, and corporate and exchange-traded funds, as well as data and connectivity services related to its exchanges and clearing houses. The Fixed Income and Data Services segment provides fixed income pricing, reference data, indices, analytics, and execution services, as well as global CDS clearing and multi-asset class data delivery technology. The Mortgage Technology segment offers a technology platform that provides customers comprehensive and digital workflow tools to address inefficiencies and mitigate risks that exist in the U.S. residential mortgage market life cycle from application through closing, servicing, and the secondary market. The company was founded in 2000 and is headquartered in Atlanta, Georgia.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jeffrey C. Sprecher | Founder, Chairman & CEO | Age 70 | Compensation: $5.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 12K people. Revenue per employee of $984K ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers, improving at 18%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $334K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $19K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 6\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Intercontinental Exchange Inc. is a large-cap financial services business with a $96.3B market cap on $12.6B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +9% over the past three years and +10% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 7% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $4.3B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 34 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.41\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 6.1\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 2.5% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 1.5\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.0) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Carries a 64% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.6358359501379769},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $11.5M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 10% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Piotroski score 8/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","12 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Financial quality scores above most Financial Services peers"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Intercontinental Exchange (NYSE:ICE) Stock: Insider Elizabeth Kathryn King Sells 1,919 Shares","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/intercontinental-exchange-nyseice-stock-insider-elizabeth-kathryn-king-sells-1919-shares.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1794005684.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.896,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Intercontinental Exchange (ICE) Draws Objections From 56 Companies Over Tokenized Stock Plan","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/diversified-financials/nyse-ice/intercontinental-exchange/news/intercontinental-exchange-ice-draws-objections-from-56-compa","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793896031.682,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.335,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Intercontinental Exchange Inc. $ICE Stake Raised by Provenance Wealth Advisors LLC","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/05/intercontinental-exchange-inc-ice-stake-raised-by-provenance-wealth-advisors-llc.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793875592.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.936,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Head-To-Head Analysis: Silvercrest Asset Management Group (NASDAQ:SAMG) vs. Intercontinental Exchange (NYSE:ICE)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/04/head-to-head-analysis-silvercrest-asset-management-group-nasdaqsamg-vs-intercontinental-exchange-nyseice.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":179384